 ## Troubleshooting
 
-- `duplicate loader entry id: skill-hub` — remove the duplicate install (keep one `dsh plugin add` method).
+- `duplicate loader entry id: dsh-skill-hub` — remove the duplicate install (keep one `dsh plugin add` method).
 - Skill missing — check the diagnostics section (frontmatter / name mismatch / short description).
 - Empty source group — its skills were deleted, or their disabled records were lost (sidecar restored/hand-edited). Startup reconciles `.disabled` files on disk; source groups with no visible member are no longer rendered.
-- Dots missing in `/` menu — dsh internals changed; catalog still works.
-- Settings card missing — it lives in the Plugins manager (sidebar → 插件 → dsh-skill-hub), not under Settings. On dsh older than `0.1.6-alpha.2` this plugin contributes no config surface at all.
+- Dots missing in `/` menu — the shell's input-trigger source registry changed; the dots ride the official candidate `icon`, so only source discovery can fail, and the catalog still works.
+- Settings card missing — it lives in the Plugins manager (sidebar → 插件 → dsh-skill-hub), not under Settings. On dsh older than `0.1.7-alpha.1` the plugin does not load at all: its settings ride the volatile `Config` extension point that release introduced.
 
