@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+# dsh-side patches (feature requests, not install requirements)
+
+This directory carries the general-purpose DeepSeek Harness changes this
+plugin's complete surface needs and cannot get from a shipped extension point.
+They are **not** required to install or run `dsh-skill-hub`: the plugin keeps a
+degrade path for every one of them (see each patch's header), which is why the
+package README can still say "no dsh source changes".
+
+Apply against a harness checkout of the matching release line
+(`dsh-v0.1.7-alpha.1` at the time of writing), from the repository root:
+
+```bash
+git apply -p1 patches/dsh-settings-section-nav-icon.patch
+git apply -p1 patches/dsh-input-trigger-sources-accessor.patch
+```
+
+| Patch | Removes this degrade path | Upstream request |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `dsh-settings-section-nav-icon.patch` | `src/client/settings-nav-icon.ts` — the scoped `MutationObserver` DOM patch that swaps the settings nav gear for the skill glyph | [discussion #1229](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness/discussions/1229), [#2864](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness/discussions/2864), [#3022](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness/discussions/3022) |
+| `dsh-input-trigger-sources-accessor.patch` | `src/client/slash-dots.tsx` — `findSkillSource()` reading the service's private `live.sources` field to wrap the core `/skill` source | no existing request; see `.dsh-migrate/patch-reports/input-trigger-sources-accessor/` |
+
+Evidence and the proposed upstream text live in
+`../.dsh-migrate/patch-reports/<slug>/report.md`.
